{"title":"Career Roadmap · Game Artist","role":"Game Artist","summary":"A Game Artist creates the visual assets that make games look and feel engaging—characters, environments, props, textures, UI elements, VFX, concept art, and sometimes animation. A B.Des in Game Design/Games Art can lead to roles across 2D art, 3D art, environment art, character art, technical art, UI art, VFX, and art direction.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Des (Bachelor of Design)","Course":"Game Design / Games Art"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["The strongest career profile combines art fundamentals","2D/3D software","game engines","portfolio","production knowledge."],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Area","Details"],"rows":[[{"text":"Degree"},{"text":"B.Des – Game Design / Games Art"}],[{"text":"Primary Career"},{"text":"Game Artist"}],[{"text":"Main Domains"},{"text":"Games, AR/VR, animation, metaverse, interactive media"}],[{"text":"Core Work"},{"text":"Characters, environments, props, textures, UI, VFX and visual assets"}],[{"text":"Major Tools"},{"text":"Blender, Maya, ZBrush, Substance 3D, Photoshop, Illustrator"}],[{"text":"Game Engines"},{"text":"Unreal Engine, Unity"}],[{"text":"Entry Roles"},{"text":"Junior 2D Artist, 3D Artist, Game Artist, Environment Artist, Character Artist"}],[{"text":"Advanced Roles"},{"text":"Senior Artist, Lead Artist, Technical Artist, Art Director"}],[{"text":"Key Differentiator"},{"text":"Strong portfolio + production-ready assets"}]]}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Game Artist can specialise into several professional tracks:"},{"type":"table","header":["Horizon","Possible Role"],"rows":[[{"text":"0–2 years"},{"text":"Junior Game Artist"}],[{"text":"2–4 years"},{"text":"3D Artist / Environment Artist / Character Artist"}],[{"text":"4–7 years"},{"text":"Senio